-- ============================================================
-- Import: B90 Row A + Row D -- real rack & device inventory
-- Source: A_Racks_B90DC.xlsx, D_Racks_B90DC.xlsx
-- Generated by Claude from the uploaded workbooks.
--
-- UPDATED for the current schema (actual power lives on the RACK,
-- not per device). Run schema.sql FIRST if you haven't already --
-- this file expects racks.actual_kva / racks.capacity_kva /
-- devices.datasheet_kva to exist.
--
-- Run this ONCE. Racks are safe to re-run (upsert by id, though a
-- re-run will NOT recompute actual_kva/capacity_kva for racks that
-- already exist -- only row_label/position are updated on conflict,
-- so a manual edit you made in-app to a rack's power figures won't
-- be overwritten by re-running this). Devices are NOT safe to
-- re-run -- it will duplicate every device row, since devices have
-- no natural unique key to upsert against. If you already ran an
-- earlier version of this file against an older schema, do not run
-- this one too -- it would duplicate every device.
--
-- If your 'b90' site doesn't exist yet, this creates it with
-- placeholder details (edit via the app's "edit site" afterward):
insert into sites (id, name, location, tier, pue)
values ('b90', 'B90', 'Cairo -- Bldg 90', 'Tier III', 1.4)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- ASSUMPTIONS MADE DURING IMPORT (please review):
-- 1. The source sheet gave one power figure (Watt) per device. Under
--    the current model that figure is stored as each device's
--    datasheet_kva (rated/nameplate spec) -- there is no per-device
--    "actual" field anymore. Each RACK's actual_kva (measured power)
--    was set to the SUM of its devices' source Watt readings,
--    converted to kVA -- this is the best available stand-in for a
--    real PDU reading; replace it with the true meter value from
--    each rack's PDU once you have it (editable from the rack's
--    detail view in the app).
-- 2. "Authorized person" = the sheet's Contact Person where present,
--    otherwise the Customer/team name (e.g. "IT Network",
--    "Security Team") as a fallback.
-- 3. Devices with no U position stated in the source were
--    auto-placed into the next free slot in that rack, in the order
--    they appeared. Their true position is unknown -- reposition
--    them in the app if you know the real slot.
-- 4. Rack capacity (max power) was set to roughly 30% headroom over
--    each rack's imported load, rounded to the nearest 5 kVA. This
--    is a placeholder -- edit each rack's real circuit rating from
--    its detail view in the app.
-- 5. A few devices' U ranges overlap another device in the SAME rack
--    -- this reflects the source data as given (e.g. a chassis
--    logged alongside the individual compute sleds inside it, or a
--    likely transcription conflict). Nothing was silently
--    corrected; review these in the app if you want strict
--    non-overlapping elevations. Racks to check: A01, A04, A05,
--    A14 (x3), A20, A23, A24, A30 (x3), D05, D06, D12, D14, D30, D33.
--
-- NOT IMPORTED (add manually if needed):
-- Passive items with no power reading in the source (patch panels,
-- ODFs/DDFs, cross-connects) were skipped since datasheet_kva must
-- be greater than 0. Six DC RECTIFIERS (B90-D02 x2, B90-D14 x2,
-- B90-D15 x2) were also skipped for this reason -- rectifiers
-- genuinely do draw real power, the source just didn't record a
-- wattage for them. These are worth adding by hand with the correct
-- figure once you have it.
-- ============================================================

